  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 143 AM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nThe large eastern US trough is approaching the eastern seaboard this \nmorning with NNW flow aloft in its wake. At the surface, high \npressure is centered over the central and southern High Plains with \na ridge axis extending northeast through IA/WI/MI. A few lake effect \nshowers will persist along the IL/IN border early this morning, \nmainly bringing a few clouds to eastern central IL this morning. The \nsurface ridge axis will drift southeast today with the high actually \nshifting east to the OH River Valley tonight. Expect light \nwinds, clear skies and the potential for frost tonight. After \nhighs in the upper 50s or so today, temps will fall through the \n50s and 40s tonight. The winds will be the limiting factor, \nkeeping temps up a bit in the western zones. However, expecting \ntemps to be in the 33 to 36 degree range generally east of I-55 \nlate tonight. In McLean Co, Bloomington/Normal may not cool \nenough for frost due to its higher elevation (it might be more \npatchy), but areas east of the cities will likely see areas of \nfrost. The further west you go, frost will be more patchy and \nlimited to valleys and areas where the wind can decrease. A \nFrost Advisory has been issued for tonight generally east of \nI-55. \n\nOn Sunday, we'll pass through \"normal\" with highs rebounding closer \nto normal/average for this time of year...the mid 60s. Sunday night \nthe surface ridge axis will extend westward from OH through IN to \nIL. So, we will likely have some rather light winds. However our low \nlevel temps will have warmed a bit, so frost shouldn't be as likely \nas it is tonight. Still, it might be close and patchy in some areas \nof east-central IL. For Monday through Friday, Illinois will see \nhighs rise through the 70s to around 80 with lows rising from around \n40 to around 50. With average highs in the mid 60s for this time of \nyear, being 15 degrees above average will be rather significant.\nBy the weekend, we'll see a system approaching with highs \nlikely peaking in the low 80s for Saturday, followed by a cold \nfront and a chance for showers Sunday night.",
